  annotation (Documentation(info = "<html><body><table><tr><td>name:</td><td>dapsone</td></tr><tr><td>ATC code:</td><td>J04BA02</td></tr><tr><td>model:</td><td>one compartment, oral dosing <small>(PK_1C_enteral)</small></td></tr><tr><td>source:</td><td>Kotila OA et al. 2023</td></tr><tr><td>population:</td><td>healthy Nigerians</td></tr><tr><td>measured compound:</td><td>dapsone</td></tr><tr><td>review:</td><td>curated candidate</td></tr><tr><td>record page:</td><td><a href=\"https://pharmacolibrary.github.io/#/drugs/drug_dapsone/Dapsone_Kotila2023_mean\">pharmacolibrary-docs</a></td></tr></table><h4>Parameters as reported in the paper</h4><table border=1 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=2><tr><th>parameter</th><th>value</th><th>unit</th><th>meaning</th></tr><tr><td>Cmax (µg/mL)</td><td>1.16</td><td>µg/mL</td><td><small>Cmax</small></td></tr><tr><td>Tmax (h)</td><td>3.77</td><td>h</td><td><small>tmax</small></td></tr><tr><td>AUC0-last (h.µg/mL)</td><td>27.7</td><td>h.µg/mL</td><td><small>AUClast</small></td></tr><tr><td>AUC0-∞ (h.µg/mL)</td><td>34.26</td><td>h.µg/mL</td><td><small>AUC∞</small></td></tr><tr><td>λz (h−1)</td><td>0.026</td><td>h−1</td><td><small>kel</small></td></tr><tr><td>t1/2z (h)</td><td>30.23</td><td>h</td><td><small>t1/2z</small></td></tr><tr><td>Cl/F (L/h)</td><td>1.69</td><td>L/h</td><td><small>CL/F</small></td></tr><tr><td>Vz/F (L)</td><td>72.18</td><td>L</td><td><small>V/F</small></td></tr><tr><td>k a</td><td>0.09</td><td>h -1</td><td><small>kabs</small></td></tr></table><h4>About dapsone</h4><p>Dapsone is used to treat leprosy, dermatitis herpetiformis, acne, and relapsing polychondritis. It remains widely used and is included on the WHO essential medicines list, with topical use for acne and systemic use for mycobacterial disease.</p><p><small>Summary written by glm-5.3-flash from <a href=\"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q422226\">Wikidata Q422226</a> and the WHO ATC classification; not checked by a person.</small></p><p>Identity, molar mass and metabolites: <a href=\"modelica://Pharmacolibrary.Drugs.Substances.Dapsone\">Dapsone</a>.</p><h4>References</h4><ol><li><p>Kotila OA et al. (2023). Non-compartmental and population pharmacokinetic analysis of dapsone in healthy NIGERIANS: A pilot study. <i>British journal of clinical pharmacology 89(11):3454–3459</i>. DOI:<a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1111/bcp.15862\">10.1111/bcp.15862</a> PUBMED:<a href=\"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/37489004\">37489004</a></p></li></ol></body></html>", revisions = "<html><body><ul><li>11/2026 generated by pharmacolibrary-dev export.pharmacolibrary_models from Kotila_2023: parameters extracted from the paper by the pharmacolibrary-dev pipeline, model built by its engineer, reviewed: curated candidate</li></ul></body></html>"),
